cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Lean 4 formalization of the Krohn–Rhodes decomposition of finite monoids into aperiodic and simple-group factors"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of the Krohn–Rhodes decomposition of finite monoids
  into aperiodic and simple-group factors: every finite monoid divides an iterated wreath
  product of finite aperiodic monoids and finite simple groups, where every simple group
  divides the monoid. Unlike the classical prime decomposition theorem, the aperiodic factors
  are not reduced to copies of the flip-flop monoid. The proof follows the local-divisor
  proof of Diekert, Kufleitner and Steinberg. The Lean definitions, statements and proofs
  were written by Claude Code agents under the direction of Aditya Rao.
type: software
authors:
